From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:31:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: ave: prioritize encoding speed by
 default

A default macOS encode session on the 14-inch MacBook Pro M4 (T8132)
runs HEVC at the encoder's maximum pixel rate: 59.6 fps at 3840x2160
and 15.2 fps at 7680x4320. Here, with the speed control at its default
of off, the firmware's throughput mode 3 gives 26.6 and 6.6 fps with
every buffer queued. That is about 45% of macOS, and the rate every
client that does not know the driver-private control gets: FFmpeg's
V4L2 encoders and the VA-API driver never set it.

With the control on (throughput mode 5), the same streams code at 48.4
and 12.4 fps (81% and 82% of macOS). On eight frames of a 4K60 clip at
30 Mb/s, PSNR moves from 54.62 to 54.49 dB at 4K and from 56.13 to
56.05 dB at 8K, with 0.6% and 2.9% more bytes.

Make the control default to on. A client that wants the quality mode
can still turn it off. H.264 is unchanged: the control has no effect
there.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-ave.rst | 6 ++++--
 drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c   | 1 +
 drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave.h        | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-ave.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-ave.rst
index 3f9b0ebf3d..946533bdcd 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-ave.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-ave.rst
@@ -148,9 +148,11 @@ Limits
   the same quality. ``BITRATE`` may change while streaming and applies from
   the next frame; ``FORCE_KEY_FRAME`` makes the next frame an IDR.
 - ``Prioritize Speed Over Quality`` (driver-private boolean,
-  ``V4L2_CID_APPLE_AVE_PRIORITIZE_SPEED`` = codec class base ``0x1200``, off by
+  ``V4L2_CID_APPLE_AVE_PRIORITIZE_SPEED`` = codec class base ``0x1200``, on by
   default) is VideoToolbox's PrioritizeEncodingSpeedOverQuality: it sets the
-  firmware's throughput mode to 5 instead of 3. It applies to HEVC (Main
+  firmware's throughput mode to 5 instead of 3. It is on by default because
+  only then does HEVC reach the rates a default macOS session reaches (4K60,
+  8K30); turn it off to code for quality at about half the rate. It applies to HEVC (Main
   and Main 10) above 1280x720 and is read when streaming starts. H.264 is not faster with it, on macOS either, so it has no effect
   there.
 - Either three B-frames or none (``B_FRAMES`` 3 or 0). H.264 Baseline and a
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
index 1c652f4719..0231923e59 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
@@ -555,6 +555,7 @@ static const struct v4l2_ctrl_config ave_ctrl_prioritize_speed = {
 	.type = V4L2_CTRL_TYPE_BOOLEAN,
 	.max = 1,
 	.step = 1,
+	.def = 1,
 };
 
 static int ave_init_ctrls(struct ave_ctx *ctx)
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave.h b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave.h
index a315570c1b..4439321382 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave.h
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ enum ave_opcode {
  * Driver-private codec-class controls.
  *
  * PRIORITIZE_SPEED is VideoToolbox's PrioritizeEncodingSpeedOverQuality:
- * off (the default) codes for quality, on trades some compression
+ * off codes for quality, on (the default) trades some compression
  * efficiency for encoding speed. It is read when streaming starts.
  */
 #define V4L2_CID_APPLE_AVE_BASE (V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_CODEC | 0x1200)
-- 
2.43.0

